From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 14:45:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: keep non-payload PPDU rates out of station_info

ath12k updates a station's visible TX bitrate for every PPDU record.  A
non-QoS PPDU or a QoS Null PPDU sent at a legacy, HE or narrow rate can
therefore replace an EHT320 data rate in station_info even though the
station remains associated with EHT capabilities.  This makes iw report an
apparent Wi-Fi 7 to Wi-Fi 6 downgrade through
NL80211_STA_INFO_TX_BITRATE while the link did not renegotiate.

Only update txrate and last_txrate for PPDUs which completed at least one
MSDU with payload bytes.  Do not use the QoS TID as a frame-type proxy:
legacy non-QoS data is valid payload and must remain visible.  The per-SKB
completion path still reports attempted payload-data rates, including
failed attempts.  Continue accumulating retry and airtime statistics for
other PPDUs so the visible-rate fix does not discard those counters.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp_rx.c
@@ -1614,6 +1614,16 @@ ath12k_update_per_peer_tx_stats(struct a
 		rcu_read_unlock();
 		return;
 	}
+
+	/* PPDUs without completed payload bytes do not describe the peer's
+	 * data rate. Account their retries and airtime without replacing it.
+	 */
+	if (!succ_pkts || !succ_bytes) {
+		arsta->tx_retry_failed += tx_retry_failed;
+		arsta->tx_retry_count += tx_retry_count;
+		arsta->tx_duration += tx_duration;
+		goto exit_unlock;
+	}
 
 	memset(&arsta->txrate, 0, sizeof(arsta->txrate));
 
@@ -1684,6 +1694,7 @@ ath12k_update_per_peer_tx_stats(struct a
 			HTT_USR_CMPLTN_SHORT_RETRY(usr_stats->cmpltn_cmn.flags);
 	}
 
+exit_unlock:
 	spin_unlock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
 	rcu_read_unlock();
 }
